%N A401874 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of simple connected graphs on n unlabeled vertices with exactly k eccentric vertices.
%C A401874 A vertex is an eccentric vertex if it is furthest away from another vertex. Every peripheral vertex is an eccentric vertex. In a tree, these are the only eccentric vertices.
%H A401874 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GraphEccentricity.html">Graph Eccentricity</a>.
%e A401874 Triangle begins:
%e A401874   1;
%e A401874   0,    1;
%e A401874   0,    1,    1;
%e A401874   0,    1,    2,    3;
%e A401874   0,    3,    2,    8,    8;
%e A401874   0,   10,   12,   16,   33,    41;
